person_id":"tvfy_10387","person_slug":"sussan-ley","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tanya Plibersek","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10513","person_slug":"tanya-plibersek","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tim Watts","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10794","person_slug":"tim-watts","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tim Wilson","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10894","person_slug":"tim-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Trent Zimmerman","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10844","person_slug":"trent-zimmerman","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Vince Connelly","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10939","person_slug":"vince-connelly","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Warren Snowdon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10599","person_slug":"warren-snowdon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zali Steggall","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10941","person_slug":"zali-steggall","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Family Assistance Legislation Amendment (Improving Assistance for Vulnerable and Disadvantaged Families) Bill 2020 - Second Reading - Keep second reading motion unchanged","noes":32,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/debate/?id=2020-08-24.120.6) to keep the original second reading motion unchanged. A [second reading motion](https://peo.gov.au/understand-our-parliament/how-parliament-works/bills-and-laws/making-a-law-in-the-australian-parliament/) is a motion \"*That this bill be now read a second time*\" - parliamentary jargon for agreeing with the main idea of the bill. This vote was put after Kingston MP [Amanda Rishworth](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/representatives/kingston/amanda_rishworth) (Labor) introduced an amendment. ### Proposed amendment > *That all words after \"That\" be omitted with a view to substituting the following words:* > > *\"whilst not declining to give the bill a second reading, the House notes that:* > > *(1) the Government will snap back to the complex and expensive child care subsidy system on 13 July and end its poorly targeted and unfunded 'free child care' response;* > > *(2) families will start paying child care fees again, even after the Treasurer admitted Australia was in a recession, and fees soared by 7.2 per cent in the last year;* > > *(3) unaffordable child care will now force families, particularly women, to reconsider returning to work and could act as a handbrake on Australia's economic recovery; and* > > *(4) early childhood workers have been ripped out of the JobKeeper program, three days after the Prime Minister promised there would be no changes until September\"*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-6472","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2020-08-24/1"}
